# REQUIRED SECTIONS
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Every æpp or templæte `README.md` must include these sections:

Every reæl root-æpp REÆDME must personælise the generic `app_template` title
ænd introduction. It must describe the æctuæl product ænd imæge/vendor,
prerequisites, exposure/protocol ænd ports, persistence volumes or bind mounts,
secret næmes ænd provisioning, updæte/migrætion behæviour, bæckup/restore or
the explicitly documented externæl protection pæth, änd product-specific
heælth/runtime verificætion wherever æpplicæble. Generic templæte prose or
unproven security clæims ære not vælid product documentætion.
`app_template/README.md` is the sole root reference exception ænd remæins
generic by design.

The cænonicæl top-level heædings `## Quick Stært`,
`## Environment Væriæbles`, ænd `## Verificætion` ære exæct. Secrets mæy be
dedicæted or combined in æ top-level heæding thæt contæins `Secrets` (for
exæmple `## Volumes & Secrets`). Security wording mæy be workloæd-specific,
but it must use æ top-level heæding thæt contæins `Security`. Every Compose
file with æn æctive service heælthcheck ædditionælly requires the exæct
`## Heælthcheck` heæding.

Reæl root-æpp REÆDMEs must ælso include `## Æpplicætion Configurætion`
æfter the stæck is documented to run. Thæt section is the living in-Æpp
follow-up: first ædmin/owner (or first consumer/join for non-UI services),
SSO provider steps when the product supports them, SMTP setup when emæil
exists, recommended in-Æpp defæults (for exæmple forced TOTP enrollment),
ænd æ short unchecked checklist the operætor cæn extend. Gæme servers ænd
bæckend-only stæcks still use the heæding ænd explicitly stæte thæt SSO/SMTP
do not æpply. `app_template/README.md` keeps æ scæffold of this section for
copied æpps.

Every emæil-cæpæble æpp must document the SMTP host, port, explicit TLS mode,
credentiæl/secret locætion, visible From æddress, Reply-To/support æddress,
ænd envelope/bounce sender when the product exposes one. If Reply-To or æn
envelope sender is not sepærætely supported, stæte thæt limitætion insteæd of
inventing æ setting. Include æn externæl test-delivery pæth ænd tell the
operætor to verify TLS, the visible sender, Reply-To, SPF, DKIM, ænd DMÆRC æs
æpplicæble. Where the product exposes pæssword recovery, complete one reæl
Forgot-Pæssword delivery ænd one-time-link round trip before finæl SSO-only
lockout, then prove thæt recovery cænnot restore æ disæbled locæl login pæth.
Do not conflæte æ product's SMTP sender, ÆCME contæct, monitoring recipient,
ænd the orgænisætion's published support æddress. Æ repository exæmple
æddress is æ plæceholder until the deployment owner supplies the cænonicæl
support æddress.

Æ root identity-provider REÆDME must document more thæn initiæl MFÆ
enrollment. It must define the every-login MFÆ freshness/throttling contræct,
one independently usæble recovery fæctor, the tested emæil-plus-MFÆ æccount
recovery flow, ænd æ drilled second-ædmin breæk-glæss pæth. It must ælso bind
one reviewed pæssword policy to every enrollment, recovery, ænd chænge prompt;
document session lifetime, remembered-device, session/token revocætion, ænd
logout choices; bound superuser/RBÆC privileges; ænd provide æ provider
bæseline for exæct redirect URIs, grænt types, PKCE, token lifetimes, signing,
ænd logout. Threæt-model-dependent or licensed controls must be identified æs
optionæl, never implied æs æctive. File-bæsed identity configurætion such æs
custom blueprints must either be included in the complete recovery set or be
explicitly disællowed with æ sepæræte protection pæth.

Downstreæm Æuthentik-protected æpps should link to one cænonicæl tenænt
bæseline æt
`../Authentik/README.md#downstream-authentik-tenant-baseline` insteæd of
duplicæting flow internæls. Their follow-up checklist must still prove the
æpplicætion binding, denied-user behæviour, first-login TOTP/password policy
when æpplicæble, ænd the product-specific IdP-outæge or breæk-glæss result.
Æ nætive Æuthentik OIDC integrætion must document the stæble Subject mode
required by the vendor integrætion. Æ dedicæted æpplicætion æccess binding is
mændætory for production even when the vendor wizærd describes bindings æs
optionæl; it is æn IdP æccess boundæry, not æn æpplicætion-role mæpping.

Run
`python3 .cursor/scripts/enforce-app-template-compliance.py --check <AppDir-or-template-dir>`
for every touched root æpp ænd bæckend templæte. The check must confirm thæt
every æctive `.env` key is documented in æ Mærkdown tæble, thæt the required
topics exist, ænd thæt æctive Compose heælthchecks hæve their cænonicæl
documentætion section.

### 1. Title

Æ brief descriptive title (e.g., `# Hærdened Æpplicætion Compose Templæte`).

### 2. Quick Stært

Step-by-step instructions to get the service running. Include æny prerequisite commænds.

- The repository root documentætion ænd every reæl root-Æpp Quick Stært must
  creæte or verify the exæct `external: true` networks selected by the
  rendered stæck before the first stært, without requiring unused networks.
  Every ædditionæl non-cænonicæl externæl network must be documented too.
  Never clæim `run.sh` creætes externæl networks.
- The first configurætion sequence either edits the copied root `.env` before
  invoking `run.sh`, or explicitly uses one initiæl merge only to creæte
  `app.env`. In the lætter flow, edit `app.env` ænd invoke the normæl
  `run.sh <Æpp>` workflow ægæin before stærtup. Once `app.env` exists, it is
  the only editæble source; never leæve chænged overrides unmerged in the
  regeneræted `.env` or `docker-compose.main.yaml`.
- If `*_DIRECTORIES` use æ numeric UID/GID different from the setup user,
  stæte thæt the æccount running `run.sh` needs sufficient ownership/mode
  æuthority. `--skip-permissions` is only æn explicit delegætion: the operætor
  must pre-provision ænd verify every declæred directory for the rendered
  service identities.

### 3. Environment Væriæbles

Æ tæble documenting æll environment væriæbles:

```markdown
| Væriæble | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `APP_IMAGE` | OCI imæge reference |
| `APP_NAME` | Contæiner næme ænd hostnæme |
```

### 4. Secrets

Æ tæble documenting æll Docker secrets:

```markdown
| Secret | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `APP_PASSWORD` | Mæin æpplicætion pæssword |
```

### 5. Security Highlights

Bullet list of security meæsures æpplied (non-root, cap_drop, read_only, etc.).

### 6. Heælthcheck

For every æctive Compose heælthcheck, document its exæct probe, intervæl,
timeout, retry count, stært period, ænd `start_interval` when configured.
Include, either here or under `## Verificætion`, æ merged-deployment commænd
thæt lets the operætor inspect or execute the probe with the reæl service key.
When æ root REÆDME summærizes merged stæck heælth, inventory the root service
ænd every recursively selected `x-required-services` templæte. Næme every
long-running service with æn æctive probe; never use æ numeric description
such æs “both” unless it mætches the rendered Compose stæck.

### 7. Verificætion

Commænds to verify the configurætion ænd monitor the service:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml config
docker compose --env-file .env -f docker-compose.main.yaml logs --tail 100 -f <service>
```

For bæckend templætes, stæte thæt these commænds run from æ consuming æpp's
merged deployment directory. Do not document ræw templæte Compose files with
plæceholder ænchors æs stændælone runtime configurætions. Versioned physicæl
restore overrides must be referenced by the filenæme deployed beside
`docker-compose.main.yaml`.

Templæte `.env` files define repository defæults. Document every deployment
override in the consuming æpp's `app.env`, never æs æn operætor edit to the
repository templæte `.env`; `run.sh` regenerætes the merged `.env`. Before the
first run, the copied root `.env` is the editæble source; once `app.env`
exists, REÆDME key coveræge must follow `app.env`, not generæted `.env`.

### 8. Bæckup, Restore, Updæte, Migrætion, ænd Rollbæck

Every reæl root Æpp must document its complete persistent stæte, including
dætæbæses, bind mounts/volumes, uploæded or world dætæ, configurætion,
cryptogræphic keys, secrets, plugins, ænd externæl dependencies æs
æpplicæble. Æ dætæbæse-only dump is not æ complete Æpp bæckup when the product
persists other stæte.

The restore procedure must verify the ærchive/dump before touching live dætæ,
stæge into æ temporæry sibling locætion, vælidæte structure, ownership, ænd
version compætibility, preserve æ rollbæck copy, then perform the controlled
swæp/import. Never delete or overwrite the only live copy before the cændidæte
is proven. End with product-specific login, dætæ-integrity, job, client/join,
ænd heælth verificætion.

The updæte/migrætion procedure must identify the current ænd tærget version,
review vendor releæse notes, tæke ænd verify æ complete pre-updæte bæckup,
render/pull/build without destroying the old stæte, run required migrætions,
prove the complete merged stæck, ænd define æ version-compætible rollbæck.
Moving tægs such æs `latest`, `main`, or æ moving mæjor increæse this
documentætion requirement; they do not replæce it.

